# Ladder authority (domain)

## Non-negotiables

- Church titles come from the **live guild roster** (`rankIndex` → `Ranks.ChurchRankIdForGuildIndex`) — never from SavedVariables commits
- Never auto-promote in WoW or in the addon — thresholds only create promote **suggestions**
- Local standing is advisory testimony — officers promote in the Blizzard guild UI
- Thresholds live only in `Data/Ranks.lua`
- Addon must not call guild promote/demote APIs

## Data flow (locked)

```
GUILD_ROSTER_UPDATE
  → Core/Roster snapshot (name → churchRankId)
  → UI Ladder refresh

events / thin Gora·Ceremony·Instance
  → Scoring (capped grants)
    → Ladder.MaybeSuggest   -- uses mapped roster rank; never auto-promote
    → Officer+ sees promote prompt
    → Officer promotes in Blizzard guild UI
    → roster refresh moves the name; suggestion auto-clears
```

## Two kinds of state

| State | Who writes | Source of truth |
|-------|------------|-----------------|
| Church title | WoW guild ranks | Live roster map |
| Local standing + suggestions | Member / officer correction | SavedVariables |

## Rank tiers (canon-driven)

- Ranks 1–5 (`kind == "points"`): threshold → `MaybeSuggest` only (prompt to promote in guild UI)
- Rank 6 (`council`) / 7 (`prophet`): never suggested from points; displayed when guild `rankIndex` maps there

## Single read path for occupants

- `Roster:GetLadderView()` / `Ladder:GetLadderView()` facade — occupants from roster only
- `GetRecord` for unknown names returns Fresh Beef **without** inserting a standing row
- Getters return **copies**

## BeefNet

- Legacy `RANK_COMMIT` / rank `SYNC_STATE` are soft-ignored — do not apply as authority
- `SUGGESTION` fanout may still notify officers of promote prompts
